      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_a3e78fc72b39350543a7d410_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "If you see __TRILIUM_PH_0__ displayed as __TRILIUM_PH_1__ or __TRILIUM_PH_2__ as __TRILIUM_PH_3__ inside a code block, that is not a replacement since replacements never run there (unless a code block is applied to an existing text). It is a __TRILIUM_PH_4__font ligature__TRILIUM_PH_5__: the default monospace font draws certain character pairs as a single symbol. The underlying text is unchanged, and copying it out gives you back __TRILIUM_PH_6__ and __TRILIUM_PH_7__.",
      "sourceHash": "a3e78fc72b39350543a7d410305d2de8f19a6a9768c88735e47e77883a0aa310",
      "context": "Automatic replacements > Characters that only look replaced (ligatures)",
      "contextHash": "81e5fdbe306a156ad342a5f24b6b3260707e903b21b2a4310bd0543fab2feff5",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_4097f1eb3cfb9e76c81aee5e_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "This can be turned off with __TRILIUM_PH_0__Options__TRILIUM_PH_1____TRILIUM_PH_2__→ Appearance → Fonts → Programming ligatures.__TRILIUM_PH_3__",
      "sourceHash": "4097f1eb3cfb9e76c81aee5e98e5b2ed869f411e5ff639ade65ef18b6dc254a9",
